Fixed text uses 584 packet tokens plus 32 completion tokens. Gating adds a mean 39.8 skipped positions: relative to fixed coding, mean goodput falls by 0.2000 bits/token [0.1805, 0.2192] and charged latency rises by 23.96 s [20.34, 27.58]. PNG goodput is identical across coders, 0.25054 bits/channel [0.24731, 0.25349], or 0.75161 bits/pixel, because all methods recover the same sources and fill the same canvas. Equal achieved rates do not imply equal capacity. Fixed PNG uses 584 packet channels; gated PNG adds 100.5 skips on average; A1 stops after a mean 597.85 channels, including 89.65 zero-bit steps. Text payloads leave a mean 162.8 padding bytes. Original charged pair times for fixed/gated/A1 are 123.33/147.29/826.57 s for text and 178.18/178.53/179.01 s for PNG, including failures.

All A1 text cases reach the 2,048-token cap with only 581--2,216 recovered packet-prefix bits (mean 1,456.85), below the 2,336-bit target. None authenticates; partial bits are not useful delivery. Independent interval and prefix audits agree across all forty prospective arithmetic cases. Two failed texts contain one and three isolated unchanged steps, each with longest run one; a successful PNG also contains one. These traces support insufficient accumulated information under the fixed cap, not sustained stagnation as the observed cause. This finite-message implementation and allocation do not demonstrate that arithmetic coding generally fails.

\subsection{Detection Depends on Carrier and Observer}
Both fixed and gated text have AUC 1.000 for both scores, with bootstrap interval [1.000, 1.000]: every steganographic score lies above the ordinary range. This complete empirical separation materially limits concealment claims, despite exact recovery. It does not imply perfect detection in a broader population. Failed A1 text has primary AUC 0.380 [0.260, 0.503]; its below-chance orientation is retained, and it delivers no payload.

Correct-context PNG mean-surprisal AUC is 0.8850 [0.7425, 0.9850] for fixed coding, 0.8300 [0.7000, 0.9375] for gating and 0.5575 [0.3750, 0.7426] for A1. Secondary log-rank AUCs are 0.8400, 0.7700 and 0.5750, respectively. Each comparison contains 20 steganographic artifacts and 20 unique controls, with none excluded. Arithmetic PNG thus combines exact recovery with lower observed separation for these scores, but its wide intervals do not establish security against arbitrary observers.

